0question","name":"support: question","color":"cccccc","default":false,"description":"Community support but can be turned into an improvement.","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":9,"created_at":"2025-06-23T22:49:34Z","updated_at":"2026-01-07T16:43:41Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"I'd like to make a `Number Field` that can also evaluate equations using [math.js](https://mathjs.org/index.html).\n\n\"5 + 20\" -> \"25\"\n\n\"sqrt(16)\" -> \"4\"\n\nIs this possible with the current `Number Field`? I can't seem to find a way to let the input accept special characters. I'd also need to extend the parse function to attempt to evaluate with math.js before the base-ui parse function takes over.\n\n\n\n\n\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/2152/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/2152/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/5114","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/5114/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/5114/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/5114/events","html_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/pull/5114","id":4733776952,"node_id":"PR_kwDOLW-eZs7qDSVg","number":5114,"title":"[password field] Create new PasswordField component","user":{"login":"atomiks","id":22450188,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIy